 for r in display:lines.append(f"|{r['name']}|{r['scope']}|{r['valid']}|{r['J_F']:.6f}|{r['duration_s']:.3f}|{r['force_peak']:.6f}|{r['moment_integral']:.6f}|{r['moment_peak']:.6f}|{r['clearance']:.9f}|")
 lines += ['', f"Confirmed improvement over inefficient student: {summary['confirmed_improvement_percent']:.3f}% ({student['J_F']-bn['J_F']:.6f} N·s). Latest complete candidate improvement: {summary['candidate_improvement_percent']:.3f}% ({student['J_F']-latest['J_F']:.6f} N·s), pending extra best confirmation. Confirmed best remains {summary['confirmed_gap_to_strong_native']:.6f} N·s above native fixed hip-leading; latest candidate remains {summary['candidate_gap_to_strong_native']:.6f} N·s above it. There is no valid matched learner result to compare with the 1344.896796 N·s matched reference. Native and matched costs never compete across scopes.", '', 'Capability is preserved at evaluated deterministic native checkpoints; there is a confirmed modest improvement over the inefficient student. Strong teacher performance is not exceeded. Latest HOLD falls from9.990 to6.580s; resulting force-integral savings include less elapsed HOLD. They are not described as pure coordination gains. PHASE_COST_DECOMPOSITION.json reports complete phase integrals and durations, with no discarded waiting.', '', f"10k candidate: OUTBOUND stopped/settled, HOLD and RETURN complete, termination COMPLETE; phase gates {latest['gates']}; safety modes {latest['safety_mode_counts']}; {latest['rejections']} reference offers rejected, modification fraction {latest['modification_fraction']:.6f}. Its full certified and physical audits are retained. ACTION_DRIFT.json records proposal-vs-anchor target-angle RMSE/peaks by phase for every evaluation, including stochastic actions. F peak has not improved over the student, and clearance decreases slightly while remaining valid.", '', '![Learning curve](LEARNING_CURVE.png)', '', '## Negative evidence and repairs', '', f"{len(negative)} invalid evaluations are retained and their partial force costs are unranked; {len(fails)} completed online episodes failed among {len(full)} full episodes. Ordinary online HOLD/RETURN failures did not automatically stop learning. Stochastic success fluctuates: point0 failed RETURN; 1k/2k/5k/10k each succeeded once, which does not establish reliable stochastic execution. Calibration failures and duplicated RNG trials remain explicit. Critic return-scale validation is weak and training gains are nonmonotonic (5k regressed near baseline). MATCHED remains ineligible; strong references remain much better.", '', 'Engineering defects discovered inside v2 are versioned, with failed traces and source histories retained: exact prediction-path float32 mismatch; duplicate calibration child seeds; generic SAC.load optimizer-group mismatch with frozen log_std (resolved by identical construction + set_parameters); collection progress loop variable overwritten by predict return; best-result nested schema indexing. Interruptions saved learning/replay/RNG state; restores verified network/target/optimizer components and did not reset counts. The interrupted217-step physical episode was archived and followed by an explicit cold boundary. These are technical resumes of the same attempt, not hidden scientific rescues. IMPLEMENTATION_REPAIRS.jsonl, IMPLEMENTATION_RESUME.jsonl, RESTORE_COMPONENT_AUDIT.json and preserved exception checkpoints document them.', '', '## Resource consumption, budgets and save state', '', f"Collection budget: 21,283 = 11,283 frozen calibration/seed + 10,000 learning; maximum50,000 was not reached. Evaluation-only interactions: {final['evaluation_only_steps']:,}, separately ledgered and not replayed except named calibration/seed collections in BUDGET.jsonl. Critic updates30,010 (20,000 warm +10,000 learning +10 small test); actor updates1,010. One attempt, zero rescues. Failed and duplicate data collection counts against the same total.", '', f"Observed online throughput median {resources['online_steps_per_s_median']:.3f} steps/s, range {resources['online_steps_per_s_range']}; warm updates ~223/s. Peak main PSS {resources['main_PSS_max_GiB']:.3f}GiB; peak new swap {resources['swap_peak_MiB']:.3f}MiB; GPU device memory reading max {resources['GPU_total_device_memory_used_max_MiB']:.0f}MiB. Minimum WSL available {resources['WSL_available_min_GiB']:.3f}GiB; minimum Windows commit headroom {resources['host_commit_headroom_min_GiB']:.3f}GiB. Resource checks did not all pass: the swap gate triggered this pause. After process exit memory was released; that does not erase the event or automatically restart training.", '', f"Training-pause wall time {pause['wall_s']/3600:.3f}h; evidence-closeout wall {wall:.3f}h, within12h. A roughly6.95h launch/end clock gap occurred around an early frozen rollout while its recorded active host duration was ~126.5s. Host/WSL suspension is a possible explanation, not established. Wall budget includes this gap; there was no extension. RESOURCE_EXTERNAL.jsonl, RESOURCES.jsonl and WORKFLOW.log retain timestamps.", '', f"Resumable checkpoint: `{pause['resumable_checkpoint']}`. It contains model.zip policy, critics/targets and both optimizer states, actor.pt, and resume.pt containing actual custom replay, immutable history hash, alpha configuration, sampler/Python/NumPy/Torch CPU/CUDA/env RNG, sample/counter state, lambda/std/lr and last-good/best metadata. RESUMABLE_STATE_AUDIT.json verifies saved components. Native SB3 replay buffer is unused; actual active replay is resume.pt. No in-flight physical rollback is claimed.", '', f"Protected old files rehashed unchanged: {len(preservation)}. Git HEAD, branch, index bytes and cached binary diff hashes remain identical. No staging, commit, push or merge. Qualified student fallback and confirmed2k actor are separately frozen; latest10k and failed candidates remain available. Full-frequency key evaluations/failures are losslessly archived; successful training stores compact actual actions/transitions. Archive hashes are in ARCHIVE_MANIFEST.json.", '', '## Evidence index and NEXT', '', '- PREREGISTRATION.json / LOCK.json: frozen scientific settings and source revision hashes.', '- RNG_ISOLATION.json / MECHANICAL_CHECKS.json: isolation, exact import and legal history checks.', '- TRANSITION_AUDIT.json / FINAL_TRANSITION_EVIDENCE_AUDIT.json: history provenance and all stored proposal/next-state checks.', '- HOLD_DIAGNOSIS.json: original complete HOLD causal trace analysis.', '- CRITIC_DIAGNOSTIC_before/after.json / UPDATES.jsonl / GRADIENT_SCALE_AUDIT.json: critic, losses, phase samples and gradient evidence.', '- ALL_EVALUATION_METRICS.json / EVALUATIONS.jsonl / NEGATIVE_RESULTS.json / ACTION_DRIFT.json: all scopes, safety/gates, failures and proposal drift.', '- PHASE_COST_DECOMPOSITION.json / LEARNING_CURVE.csv/.png/.pdf: full phase cost/time evidence.', '- RESOURCE_PAUSE_REQUEST.json / RESOURCE_PAUSE_CLOSEOUT.json / RESUMABLE_STATE_AUDIT.json: exact pause, completed evaluations and pending confirmation.', '- FINAL_PRESERVATION.json / ARCHIVE_MANIFEST.json: readonly preservation and final evidence hashes.', '', 'Heavy simulation/training remains paused at the requested resource exception. If a later continuation is authorized and resources meet the original gates, use the complete paused learning state, retain21,283 consumed collection steps, and reconcile/finish pending10k capability bookkeeping and extra best replay before further actor updates. Do not blindly restart failed actors, reset budgets, loosen thresholds or automatically resume merely because memory fell after exit. The original12h run deadline is not extended by this closeout. This workflow stops here.', '', 'STOP.']
 report='\n'.join(lines)+'\n'
